# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in the value. .env.local is ignored by
# git and is the only place the real key should ever live.

# Web3Forms access key for the contact form.
#
# WHAT THIS IS: a public identifier issued by Web3Forms, tied to the single
# address enquiries are delivered to (aetextechsolutions@gmail.com). Because
# the form posts directly from the browser to the provider, this value ships in
# the JavaScript bundle. That is how the provider is designed to work, and it
# is why the key is not treated as a secret: it can only cause a submission to
# be delivered to the address it is already registered against. It cannot read
# mail, change the destination, or send anywhere else.
#
# WHAT THIS IS NOT: a Gmail password, a Gmail app password, an SMTP credential,
# or any private server secret. None of those belong in this file, in any
# VITE_-prefixed variable, or anywhere else in this repository — every VITE_
# variable is compiled into the client bundle and is readable by anyone.
#
# To obtain one: create a Web3Forms account using aetextechsolutions@gmail.com,
# verify the address, and copy the access key it issues.
VITE_WEB3FORMS_ACCESS_KEY=your-web3forms-access-key-here
